            "body": "seems #43732 fixed the same issue the opposite way: the scheduler binds with `same_port=True`, so it never moves, and the server that loses the race fails at startup.\r\n\r\nHowever I believe in RL case (and most other cases), the losing server should still start, bind a free port and report it faithfully as this PR does.\r\n(except for explicit `--scheduler-port` or `--strict-ports`, where `same_port=True` so port should never be moved)",
